{"name":"Billiard Table","hex":"#155843","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"billiard table","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy felt-covered table fitted with six pockets along the perimeter used in the games of pool, billiards or snooker."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/billiard_table"}],"entries":[{"title":"Billiard table","blocks":[{"text":"A billiard table or billiards table is a bounded table on which cue sports are played. In the modern era, all billiards tables provide an elevated flat surface usually made of quarried slate, that is covered with cloth, and surrounded by vulcanized rubber cushions. More specific terms are used for specific sports, such as snooker table and pool table, and different-sized billiard balls are used on these table types. An obsolete term is billiard board, used in the 16th and 17th centuries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/A_carom_table_in_Caf%C3%A9_Z%C3%A9phyr%2C_Paris%2C_France%2C_14_January_2007.jpg/330px-A_carom_table_in_Caf%C3%A9_Z%C3%A9phyr%2C_Paris%2C_France%2C_14_January_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billiard_table","wikidata":"Q3500725"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/%22Billiard_Table_Manufactory%2C_J._M._Brunswick_%26_Bro.%2C_Proprietors%2C_Cincinnati%2C_Ohio%22_1865_ad_in_Polk%27s_Nashville_%28Davidson_county%2C_Tenn.%29_City_Directory_..._1865_%28IA_polksnashvilleda00nash%29_%28page_10_crop%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/%22Billiard_Table_Manufactory%2C_J._M._Brunswick_%26_Bro.%2C_Proprietors%2C_Cincinnati%2C_Ohio%22_1865_ad_in_Polk%27s_Nashville_%28Davidson_county%2C_Tenn.%29_City_Directory_..._1865_%28IA_polksnashvilleda00nash%29_%28page_10_crop%29.jpg/1280px-thumbnai